WEBVTT

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:35.370
Subtitles by the Amara.org community

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:08.060
What a horrible accident!

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.060
Call an ambulance, now!

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:13.050
I'm leaving!

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:27.450
I was not to blame!

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:30.000
Yusuke Urameshi, 14 years old.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:43.980
the hero of the story but suddenly, unfortunately, dies.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:49.840
Brazilian version, Audio News Rio.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:50.980
That's the cure?

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:52.310
That victim over there isn't me?

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:03.620
Excuse me.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:11.780
The child is fine, she just had a scratch.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:14.850
The boy is good.

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:17.800
Let's put him on the stretcher.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.800
Hey, wait a minute there.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.800
And we're going to take the child too.

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:27.270
Hey friend, wait a minute.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:29.110
You're exaggerating, boy. I'm here, I'm alive here.

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:30.000
Look, I'm here.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.000
Look, don't you see me? You're...

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.000
You crazy bastard!

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:47.010
What's going on?

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:48.010
I don't understand a thing.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:50.180
There's a lot of calm at this hour, I have to remember.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:56.000
If I'm not mistaken, today I went to school after 10 days.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.000
I'm Kyo Kurameshi, Professor Takenaka is waiting for you.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.800
You're not in the meeting room.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:11.680
Keiko, what do you want?

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:14.880
I knew you were here.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:19.900
Look at your criminal.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:20.900
You better stop this.

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.700
You think you're going to keep killing classes?

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:25.410
Keiko, I'm fed up with your sermons, okay?

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.610
But you're going to hear how many times I want to talk.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:30.000
And if you keep doing this, you're going to repeat it for years.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:33.820
Kenaka's calling you to his room.

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:36.820
At least he must have prepared something to be called there.

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:39.820
And if you don't go, I'll take the blame for being the class representative.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:42.820
I think it's good you go before I get bored with you, got it?

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:46.190
Do you understand me?

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:50.930
She's white, but she's kind of dirty.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:57.840
You idiot, you bastard, you idiot, you're shameless!

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:04.490
He's a fat guy, apparently he didn't change his mind at all.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:09.650
Keiko, how was it?

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:12.250
What are you doing in the corner?

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:15.400
We're really scared of Yusuke.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:19.490
Can you talk to him properly?

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:23.490
Keiko, if you keep talking to him, you're going to hurt yourself.

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:24.830
Oh, what's that?

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:27.970
He's a fat guy, shameless, but he doesn't hurt anyone.

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:30.000
Sometimes he's a cool guy.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.980
But his fame is the worst possible, Keiko.

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:35.980
Sometimes the colleges want to take Urameshi anyway.

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:38.980
It's true, Keiko. They say he's already gathered 2,000 bandits.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:41.980
Oh, that's nothing. That's just a joke.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:42.980
What?

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:45.980
2,000 bandits? Damn, that's too much.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:48.980
He doesn't even gather two people. He almost has no friends.

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:52.130
I don't take risks. And I'm still afraid.

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:58.710
Urameshi, Urameshi, immediately appear in the orientation room.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.750
What an annoying comrade, be serious.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.950
Damn, you'll get a lot of money.

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:13.600
It was perfect, some guys came to bother me and I lied saying I was Uramesh's cousin.

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:16.960
Brave, if he finds out, you'll be in big trouble.

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:19.840
Oh, that's nothing.

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:22.930
Just take him that way, talk to him, he'll fall right down.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:31.990
Yusuke, it was bad, Yusuke!

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:34.310
It was bad, man!

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:39.170
Ah, you're just playing, aren't you?

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:42.000
What are you doing there?

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:45.000
Thank goodness, Professor.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:48.560
You can stay calm. What did he do to you?

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.800
He didn't do anything, no.

00:06:55.760 --> 00:07:00.000
Ah, and by any chance, is this brute scaring you, this great beast?

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:02.370
And the guy?

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:05.670
From now on, you don't need to come to school anymore!

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:07.430
Get out of here!

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:10.470
Don't fill me, I'll do whatever I want, okay?

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:24.910
I'll throw you, it's a joke.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:30.000
Damn it!

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:32.280
Listen here, you...

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:34.840
Stop calling me professor, respect me.

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:37.840
You, by any chance, didn't hear my call?

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:41.700
I did hear it, even your voice is cute, but they sent me away and I'm leaving.

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:44.780
Something must have happened.

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:46.860
Wait, I didn't do anything.

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.700
Let's go to the orientation room.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:55.640
Keep in mind that you're only going home at night. Are you listening?

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:56.600
Huh?

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:59.800
Huh?

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:01.920
It's just a toy earring.

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:04.900
Now get out of my way, okay? Forget about me!

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:08.460
Come back here! Come back here!

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.510
Okay, but it only happens to me.

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:14.910
Every day I'm excited to go to school, everyone fills me with patience.

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:15.910
Damn it!

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:18.080
It makes me angry, man!

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:25.600
Okay, I can't believe it. Are you waking up now, mom?

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:27.750
Make me a coffee.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:29.670
Okay, I'll do it.

00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:34.900
- And the school, huh? - Oh, I missed it. I'm not in the mood.

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:40.500
If you don't feel like it, stop it now. The school is not for free, you know?

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:44.950
Come on, you're going to give me a sermon now, mom? Stop it, please, right?

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:50.290
Gustavo, go get a job, you vagabond.

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:59.160
There are days when we shouldn't even have left bed. Seriously!

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:16.900
But you are very bad, huh? You don't get tired of getting beaten up, do you?

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:19.720
Shut up! Let's take a cracker and see who's better.

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:21.940
I'm the strongest in the Saralha-Chique school.

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:26.200
You're going to kneel and lick my feet, got it?

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:30.000
The only problem is that you caught me one day,

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:32.030
I woke up with legs that...

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:45.780
Oh, Devil!

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:52.150
Now I'm in a good mood.

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:56.150
Kuwabara, haven't I told you to stop challenging Uramesh?

00:09:56.150 --> 00:10:00.000
You've already lost to him 156 times!

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:05.100
Shut up, I won't give up, until I win!

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:12.770
After that, I found the little boy.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:20.840
Uncle!

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:24.230
Thank you very much, Mr. Zé Mané.

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:27.430
It's dangerous to play here. The cars will catch you, you know?

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:41.230
"What a strange guy!"

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:50.610
"I'm glad I didn't lose the clown's eye."

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:54.770
"Look at the little ball. Don't play on the street anymore, okay?"

00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:57.770
"It can be very dangerous. Go play at home, in a safe place."

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:15.130
What a stubborn boy! I've already sent him home, but he wants to keep playing on the street!

00:11:15.130 --> 00:11:27.330
No, boy, don't go to the street! Please, be careful!

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:53.530
I remembered. I was run over and died. But what am I doing here?

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:57.300
Oh, it can't be. Could it be...

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:59.740
Could it be that I become a child?

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:09.920
You understood fast, you're smart.

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:26.160
It's you.

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:30.000
When people die in accidents, souls don't believe they died.

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:32.690
Then they wander the world without going anywhere.

00:12:32.690 --> 00:12:34.270
Forget it, I want to know who you are.

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:37.490
My name is Botan, I am the guide who guides the San Zu crossing,

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:39.490
the river of hell, to the spiritual world.

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:42.490
I am the Goddess of Death, as Westerners say.

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:43.490
Nice to meet you.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.330
Nice to meet you, I'll show you "nice to meet you".

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:47.330
What the hell is this?

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:50.830
Look here, I hope you don't be rude to me, okay?

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:54.160
Yeah, Kiko says I'm a little rude, yes.

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:55.160
But I'm very shocked.

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:57.050
Your happiness is annoying me, you know?

00:12:57.050 --> 00:12:58.050
Huh?

00:12:58.050 --> 00:13:00.000
You should be sad, that's regrettable.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:00.900
I'm shocked!

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:03.590
Instead of being scared, you threaten me!

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:07.590
Wow, your character matches exactly what is in the Ema file.

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:08.590
Let me see.

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:10.590
Ah, Yusuke Urameshi, 14 years old.

00:13:10.590 --> 00:13:13.590
is rude, is violent, is impatient, is daring.

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:15.590
In addition, he is a thief and a fool.

00:13:15.590 --> 00:13:17.590
Oh my God, even that!

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:21.590
Maybe it would have been better if you had really died, you know?

00:13:21.590 --> 00:13:23.590
Hello, great deduction!

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:30.000
Listen here, girl. Let's stop talking nonsense.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.890
I'm worried about the little boy.

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:33.910
What happened to him, huh?

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:37.050
We can check.

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:44.250
He just scratched his forehead and arms.

00:13:44.250 --> 00:13:46.250
Nothing happened to his head and bones.

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:48.630
That's good, Masaru.

00:13:48.630 --> 00:13:53.920
Ah, so it's okay. I don't need to worry anymore.

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:56.070
Now you can complete your work.

00:13:56.070 --> 00:13:59.080
Because I'm not even there. You can take me wherever you want.

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:03.140
What's the matter, blue hair? What is it?

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:05.160
You're completely mistaken.

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:07.160
Scooter didn't come here to pick you up.

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:12.160
I just wanted to know if you want to do the Resurrection Test to come back to life.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:14.140
Come back to life? Test?

00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:15.280
Yeah.

00:14:15.280 --> 00:14:17.250
Come here, can you explain or is it hard?

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:23.610
Well, here's the deal. In fact, your death was not expected by the spiritual world.

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:24.530
And?

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:30.000
You know what it is? It's that even God didn't imagine that you would give your life to save a child.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.820
so there's no place for you in heaven or hell.

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:35.280
Okay, I said it, okay?

00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:37.280
What nonsense is this about no place?

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:39.480
There's no reason. I gave my life to save that child.

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:41.280
That wasn't planned, was it?

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:45.360
I didn't say that before, because you could be very shocked.

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:49.280
But actually, that child was destined to be run over.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:53.080
And it would miraculously come out whole, without any scratch.

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:55.370
Without... without any scratch?

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:57.870
Yeah, I'm sorry. That's it.

00:14:57.870 --> 00:15:00.000
It's... it's very...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:03.000
It's really hard to say this, but your death was in vain.

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:09.520
You were shocked, right? You were shocked, yes!

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:12.410
But look, don't get angry, okay?

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:14.840
Calm down, because you'll have another chance.

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:18.840
And it's very simple, you just need to do the Resurrection Test.

00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:25.640
And look what a privilege, this happiness is only granted to 1% of the population.

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:29.700
Ah, the Resurrection Test, that's nonsense, I'm out.

00:15:38.090 --> 00:15:40.650
Even if you don't listen!

00:15:40.650 --> 00:15:41.880
Nonsense!

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:46.900
Listen, little blue hair, I'm not even there.

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:48.980
Yeah, I'd rather stay as a ghost.

00:15:48.980 --> 00:15:52.370
Because even if I come back, I have nothing to gain.

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:56.950
Yeah, to tell the truth, people must be happy that I died.

00:15:56.950 --> 00:15:59.320
And if I resurrect, no one will like it.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:04.000
Besides, I think mom can lead a much calmer life without me.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:06.920
How sad to hear that from a 14-year-old boy.

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:10.920
Yeah, that's why I'd rather not do this test, little blue hair.

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:14.990
Look, you don't have to answer now.

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:19.990
You can watch your schedule first, think a lot, and then decide.

00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:24.230
My decision is already made!

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:41.560
Hey, look, it's the school's guys.

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:47.370
What a shameless gang, they're happy with my death!

00:16:48.010 --> 00:16:53.750
Keiko, why did he leave me?

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:58.550
Oh, I don't know why, all this crying.

00:17:02.240 --> 00:17:04.480
- Calm down. - Relax, Kuwabara.

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:06.680
- Leave me alone! Leave me alone! - Calm down, calm down.

00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:08.560
- Wait. - Leave me alone!

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:12.190
- You have to respect me. - Huh? It's Kuwabara!

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:16.800
Ah, that was your suggestion. You died without giving me a refund.

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:23.520
- Kuwabara, we're in a veloid. - Listen here, Urameshi, are you listening to me?

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:28.010
- I promised to kill him, are you listening? - He's dead. He can't hear you.

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:30.000
Resurrect, damn it!

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:32.270
Come and fight me!

00:17:32.270 --> 00:17:35.170
And now, who's gonna fight me?

00:17:36.170 --> 00:17:38.620
I want you to move, you bastard!

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:40.620
I'm never gonna forgive you!

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:45.520
Repit the game, you bastard!

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:46.520
Repit!

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:47.660
Repit!

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:54.100
Let's go back.

00:18:03.610 --> 00:18:06.650
But who are they?

00:18:06.650 --> 00:18:09.650
It's the heavy class. They like to tumultuate everything.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:13.350
They are immoral children.

00:18:13.350 --> 00:18:16.920
But fortunately one of them died practicing something good.

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:18.920
And that helped improve the fame of our school.

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:20.920
I already know what could have happened.

00:18:20.920 --> 00:18:26.810
Maybe he pushed the boy like a clown and by accident ended up being run over by a car.

00:18:26.810 --> 00:18:29.190
That is quite possible, professor.

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:32.940
Oh, you sons of bitches! I want to see you talk in front of me!

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:40.820
Now I want you to tell me what is more immoral,

00:18:40.820 --> 00:18:43.700
his action or your conversation.

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:06.890
I was surprised to know that you saved a child.

00:19:06.890 --> 00:19:15.350
But I don't know why I don't want to praise what you did.

00:19:19.490 --> 00:19:23.460
Death is the end of everything.

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:48.820
to be able to

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:28.740
He was like this when he woke up.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:49.110
You've decided?

00:20:49.110 --> 00:20:51.120
Listen, Botan.

00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:52.280
What is it?

00:20:52.280 --> 00:20:57.400
How is this test of the resurrection? What kind of test is this?

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:59.400
To tell you the truth, I don't know.

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:02.310
Are you going to do it?

00:21:02.310 --> 00:21:04.930
I will, yes.

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:07.760
Come with me!

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:14.660
Hello, very calm at this time!

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:16.660
Listen here, where are you taking me?

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:18.660
To another world!

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:20.160
To another world?

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:23.930
I'm going to find the person who will explain the test to you.

00:21:23.930 --> 00:21:28.810
Come with me, but for the love of God, without answering, huh?

00:21:28.810 --> 00:21:30.000
When did you get to Paris?

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:36.860
To participate in the story, Yusuke ended up dying, but he will have to go through the resurrection test to continue living.

00:21:36.860 --> 00:21:47.860
But how will this test be?

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:53.590
I don't know what kind of test I'm going to undergo. I just know that if I overcome it, I'm going to live again.

00:21:53.590 --> 00:21:56.990
But if my body is burned, then I'm screwed.

00:21:56.990 --> 00:22:00.000
I can't count on my mother, right?

00:22:00.860 --> 00:22:06.150
There is no other way, I have to ask help from Keiko, but how am I going to do that?

00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:12.770
Next episode in the Spiritual World, test of the resurrection, I did not know the other world on purpose!

00:22:30.190 --> 00:22:55.110
And the bridge-bearers are chasing you back, listening to you follow.

00:23:00.670 --> 00:23:16.610
Without stopping, I dream
